3.	STAKEHOLDERS AND DECISION MAP
3.1	Stakeholder Identification

Lecturer -	Review AI recommendation
Academic - Advisor	Provides academic follow up
Student -	Person affected by the decision
System Administrator -	Maintains the software
AI Developer -	Develop, train and test the AI model


3.2	Stakeholder Needs

3.2.1	Lecturers
•	Recommendations that are easy to understand
•	A quick access to student information
•	Accurate analysis
•	Explanation for the indicators
•	The ability to override the AI suggestion when needed.

3.2.2	Academic Advisors
•	A record of student risk history 
•	Evidences that back up the recommendation from the AI
•	Records of the previous interventions

3.2.3	Student
•	Fair Treatment among all
•	Privacy protections
•	Human oversight for important decisions

3.2.4	System Administrator
•	A secure System that protect student data
•	Simple and practical deployment
•	System monitoring

3.2.5	AI Developer
•	Access to relevant academic data for model development
•	Reliable model evaluation results
•	Ability to monitor prediction performance and model drift
•	Model version control and documentation


3.3	Decision to be Supported

The AI-assisted system support the decision of the lecturers or academic advisor to review the students academic performance for possible academic support. The AI-assisted system does not decide whether the students fail the semester or subject or disciplinary action should be taken for missing assignment submission and missing classes or whether the student should be removed from the programme.

3.4	Decision Authority

The final decision should be made by a human which in this case are the lecturers and academic advisors. The AI-assisted system shouldn’t have the authority to make decision and just need to analyze and provide recommendations to the academic staff.

3.5	Human Oversight

Human oversights are needed at a certain point of the process in which are:

•	Review the input data to the AI-assisted system
•	Review the prediction made by the AI-assisted system
•	Review the evidence and explanation made by the AI-assisted system
•	Final decision on whether intervention is needed
•	Override the AI-assisted system recommendation if proved intervention is not needed

3.6	Accountability

The accountabilities are distributed as below:

Responsibility	Accountable Party
Data Correctness	Data Owner
Model Development	Development Team
System Operation	System Administrator
Academic Decision	Lecturer or Academic Advisor


3.7	Affected Parties

The primary affected parties are students. Because if the system performed correctly the student will show positive improvement in their study, but if the system perform incorrectly, the student may show negative impact such as further decline in their study. Therefore, fairness, privacy, transparency and huma oversight are essential key to provide a positive outcome.

 
